{"comments":"FPS — Frames per second atom for animation and video timing.\n\nRepresents the rate at which frames are displayed or processed.\nUsed in motion graphics, video editing, game loops, and animation.\n\n## Common Frame Rates\n\n- **24 fps**: Cinema standard\n- **25 fps**: PAL television\n- **29.97 fps**: NTSC television (drop-frame timecode)\n- **30 fps**: NTSC simplified / web video\n- **48 fps**: High frame rate cinema (HFR)\n- **50 fps**: PAL high-quality\n- **59.94 fps**: NTSC high-quality\n- **60 fps**: Games, smooth animation\n- **120 fps**: High-end displays, VR\n- **144/240/360 fps**: Gaming monitors\n","declarations":[{"children":[{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Eq"],"Eq"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Temporal","FPS"],"FPS"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[72,32],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Temporal/FPS.purs","start":[72,1]},"title":"eqFPS"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Ord"],"Ord"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Temporal","FPS"],"FPS"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[73,34],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Temporal/FPS.purs","start":[73,1]},"title":"ordFPS"},{"comments":null,"info":{"declType":"instance","dependencies":[],"type":{"annotation":[],"contents":[{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Data","Show"],"Show"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"},{"annotation":[],"contents":[["Hydrogen","Schema","Temporal","FPS"],"FPS"],"tag":"TypeConstructor"}],"tag":"TypeApp"}},"sourceSpan":{"end":[76,42],"name":"../src/Hydrogen/Schema/Temporal/FPS.purs","start":[75,1]},"title":"showFPS"}],"comments":"Frames per second (> 0)\n\nBounded by construction. Zero or negative FPS cannot exist.\nMinimum is 0.01 fp